From 630e1a07cae63a3b28c955d1d9f166a6c0de3628 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:50:45 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH v2 0/8] ksmbd: improve READ sends and WRITE execution

This series reduces TCP READ payload copies and routes eligible WRITEs to
a CPU-scoped, non-strict unbound workqueue. Completed WRITE responses are
coalesced without waiting to fill a batch.

The last two patches are separate, default-off experiments: per-connection
placement based on observed WRITE overlap, and sending completed WRITE
responses from the TCP receiver. The startup WRITE policy also requires
companion ksmbd-tools support.

The latest short comparison used tmpfs, 1 MiB single-channel WRITEs,
libaio/direct=0/cache=none, on a 128-CPU server with a local 4-vCPU client.
Server CPUs used schedutil except client host CPUs16-23, which retained
performance in every arm. Two paired rounds used 15s warmup, 2s ramp and
30s measurement, without tracing. READ splice was off in all three arms.

Throughput (MiB/s):

 jobs  QD   PERCPU   Adaptive/worker TX   Adaptive/RX TX   RX/PERCPU
    1   2  2792.07             2587.08          3081.68     +10.37%
   16  32  2181.93             3364.07          3793.72     +73.90%

Percentages are medians of within-round changes. All arms used the same
module/core; PERCPU is the disabled-optimization path, not a separately
built historical stock kernel. QD2 P99 improved by 41.27% over PERCPU;
high-concurrency P99 did not consistently improve over worker-owned TX.

Bounded invalid-session response tests covered FIN, paused reads/resume
and RST cleanup. RX-owned sending can still block on TCP send backpressure;
nonblocking send coordination remains open. These short tests do not yet
establish behavior across mixed traffic, multiple channels and low QDs.

Huiwen He (8):
  workqueue: export attribute and sysfs setup helpers
  ksmbd: route WRITE requests to an unbound workqueue
  ksmbd: complete TCP frames before reporting send success
  ksmbd: send READ payloads with MSG_SPLICE_PAGES
  ksmbd: coalesce completed WRITE responses
  ksmbd: accept WRITE workqueue policy from startup configuration
  ksmbd: experiment with per-connection WRITE placement
  ksmbd: experiment with RX-owned WRITE response sending

